! C22-6578 PROBLEM 4.6, "TRANSPOSITION OF AN 8 x 8 BIT MATRIX", printed
! p.39 (PDF 40), Method 1, read in the ink at 300 dpi.
!
!   "Given an 8x8 matrix whose elements are bits stored consecutively
!   and row-wise starting at BMATX8.  Create the transpose and store the
!   latter in the same area."
!
!   "Method 1.  Bit-by-bit operation"
!   Comments: "(a) The program is written to accommodate an NxN bit
!   matrix beginning at LOC.  The SYN pseudo-instructions define LOC as
!   BMATX8 and N to be 8.  BMATX8 is assumed to be defined elsewhere in
!   the symbolic program.  (b) 0.N is equivalent to 0.8, since N is 8."
!
! THE EIGHTEEN PRINTED STATEMENTS FROM BMX8T TO "N SYN,8" ARE AS
! PRINTED.  The deck defines BMATX8, between two guard words.  Assembled
! by the host STRAP II (ASM=strap2).  Problem 4.7 Method 1 is this
! program "with LOC and N redefined to be BMX64 and 64": deck
! problem_4_7_method1.strap.
!
! "N($3)" IS RIGHT AS PRINTED, though it looks like a missing "0.": in a
! VFL instruction's 24-bit address field an integer counts bits
! (C28-6129 Section I printed pp.8-9, "INTEGER ADDRESSES"; C22-6531 the
! same table), so N($3) advances $3 by eight bits, one row.
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES, by the Reference Manual (22-6530-2; printed page
! = PDF - 3):
!   LF and SF are connectives: LF = C0011, SF = CM0101 (C28-6129
!   Appendix C printed p.50; strap_asm's CONNECTIVE_ALIASES has the
!   listings that confirm both).  0011 is "m" and 0101 is "a" (Figure 20,
!   printed p.76).  With field length 1 and the default byte size 8 the
!   one byte is short: "only those bits ... included in the field length
!   take part" (printed p.75), so each moves exactly one bit, and
!   CONNECT leaves "the remainder of the accumulator ... unchanged".
!
!   LF(BU,1),0.0($3),64   bit at $3 into accumulator bit 63 (offset 64:
!                         right end 64 bits from bit 127).
!   LF(BU,1),0.0($2)      bit at $2 into accumulator bit 127.
!   SF(BU,1)(V+ICR),0.1($2),64   bit 63 to $2's place; $2 += 0.1,
!   SF(BU,1)(V+ICR),N($3)        bit 127 to $3's place; $3 += 0.8:
!                         the two bits are exchanged.  Each counts its
!                         index down and refills it at zero (printed
!                         p.21).
!   BZXCZ, LOF            while $3's count is not zero.
!   V+C,$2,VF; V+C,$3,VF  add VF's value, 0.1+0.N = 0.9, and count down
!                         (printed p.24); SX keeps each as its refill.
!
!   XW2 = LOC+0.1 (A[0][1]), XW3 = LOC+0.8 (A[1][0]), counts N-1 = 7,
!   refills XW22 and XW33, which the first line fills from XW2 and XW3.
!   Row i starts at $2 = LOC + 0.(9i+1), $3 = LOC + 0.(9i+8), count 7-i:
!   the inner loop exchanges A[i][j] and A[j][i] for j = i+1..7 and is
!   refilled to the row's start, V+C moves both to the next row's first
!   element above (below) the diagonal and takes the count to 6-i.  Row
!   6 leaves count 0 and the second BZXCZ falls to BEW.  28 exchanges,
!   each pair above the diagonal once.
!
! THE DATA AND THE EXPECTED VALUES, worked by hand:
!
!      BMATX8 as loaded               its transpose
!      0 0 1 1 1 1 0 0   3C           0 1 0 1 1 0 0 1   59
!      1 0 0 1 1 1 1 0   9E           0 0 0 0 1 1 1 0   0E
!      0 0 0 1 0 1 0 1   15           1 0 0 1 0 1 0 0   94
!      1 0 1 0 0 1 1 1   A7           1 1 1 0 1 0 0 0   E8
!      1 1 0 1 0 0 1 0   D2           1 1 0 0 0 0 1 1   C3
!      0 1 1 0 0 0 0 0   60           1 1 1 1 0 0 0 1   F1
!      0 1 0 0 1 0 1 1   4B           0 1 0 1 1 0 1 1   5B
!      1 0 0 0 1 1 1 1   8F           0 0 1 1 0 0 1 1   33
!
!   BMATX8 (200.0)   (16)590E94E8C3F15B33
!   x2 (18)          row 6 refilled to 200.55 count 1, V+C: 200.55 +
!                    0.9 = 201.0, count 0, refill XW22 (word 44):
!                    (16)003240000000002C.  In general LOC + N*N bits.
!   XW22             the same word: SX after the last V+C.
!   x3 (19)          200.62 + 0.9 = 201.7, count 0, refill XW33 (word
!                    45): (16)003247000000002D.  In general LOC + N*N +
!                    N - 1 bits.
!   XW33             the same word.
!   acc_left (8)     bit 63 holds A[7][6] of the matrix as loaded, the
!                    last bit LF brought from $3: 1, and nothing else was
!                    ever written into the left half (it starts 0).
!   acc_right (9)    bit 127 holds A[6][7] as loaded: 1.
!   guards           unchanged.  PC: 82, the half word of the printed BEW.
!   Index words: value bits 0-23 (bit address) and sign 24 (printed
!   p.21), count 28-45 and refill 46-63 (printed p.24).
!
! PASSED AGAINST THE MODEL AS IT STOOD (run line in tests/run_tests.sh).
!
! INJECTION, DATA SIDE, OBSERVED 2026-11-16 (a private copy of the deck):
!   BMATX8's first byte 3C -> 1C (A[0][2] turned off), the program and
!   the checks untouched.  PREDICTED: the transpose's third byte, column 2,
!   94 -> 14 (A[0][2] is now row 2's bit 0).
!   OBSERVED: FAIL BMATX8_transposed only (got (16)590E14E8C3F15B33); the
!   index words, XW22/XW33, the accumulator, the guards and the PC pass.

! --- printed p.39, Method 1 -------------------------------------------
BMX8T   LX, $2, XW2; SX, $2, XW22
        LX, $3, XW3; SX, $3, XW33
LOF     LF(BU,1),0.0($3),64
        LF(BU,1), 0.0($2)
        SF(BU,1)(V+ICR),0.1($2),64
        SF(BU,1)(V+ICR),N($3)
        BZXCZ,LOF
        V+C,$2, VF; SX,$2,XW22
        V+C, $3, VF; SX, $3,XW33
        BZXCZ, LOF
        BEW,$
XW2     XW, LOC+0.1,N-1,XW22
XW3     XW,LOC+0.N,N-1, XW33
XW22    XW,0
XW33    XW,0
VF      VF,0.1+0.N
LOC     SYN, BMATX8
N       SYN,8
! --- the deck's data ---------------------------------------------------
        SLC, 199.0
GUARD1  DD(BU,64),(16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
BMATX8  DD(BU,64),(16)3C9E15A7D2604B8F
GUARD2  DD(BU,64),(16)5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A
        END, BMX8T
